\fs20
\b Endpoint Platform Agent\b0\par
\par
This software is installed and operated under the terms agreed between your organisation and the operator of the Endpoint Platform management server it connects to.\par
\par
\b What this agent does\b0\par
\par
It reports hardware, software, update and local-account inventory to the management server, and applies management tasks that the server authorises. It runs as a Windows Service under the LocalSystem account, because creating and modifying local Windows accounts requires administrative privilege.\par
\par
\b Network\b0\par
\par
The agent makes outbound HTTPS connections to the management server only. It does not accept inbound connections, and it does not require this computer to share a network with the management server or with any other managed computer.\par
\par
\b What it does not do\b0\par
\par
It does not execute arbitrary commands, scripts or shell input from the server. Every action it can take is one of a fixed, published set of typed operations.\par
